  "id": "analog-computer",
  "term": "analog computer",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, an analog computer is a way of describing human cognition as continuous, resonating, interconnected circuits rather than separate digital-like modules. On this view, the mind constantly draws information from a complex, changing environment to build an internal model of reality for rapid response.",
